"explanation": "To neutralize an acidic substance, a basic (alkaline) substance is required. On the pH scale, values below 7 are acidic, 7 is neutral, and values above 7 are basic. Among the options, baking soda has a pH of 8-9, making it the only basic substance. Citrus fruit is highly acidic (pH 2-3), while dairy and water are near-neutral to slightly acidic. Therefore, baking soda is the most effective option for neutralizing an acidic food.",
